# ---- weekly restore drill (#400, BH-1731) ------------------------------------
# bin/restore-drill.sh (hub, Sundays 06:00Z) borrows a fresh Orgo computer,
# runs the drill steps on it (drill_on_box, bin/lib/restore-drill-steps.sh) and
# deletes it again, then beats `restore-drill: OK|FAIL|SKIP <detail> RPO=<age>`
# and writes state/restore-drill-last.json.
#   OK   the steps returned 0 AND said OK.
#   FAIL something broke: the create, the wait, the steps, or a leaked box from
#        a previous run that would not delete. Until #1732 lands the steps are a
#        stub, so every armed run FAILs `steps not implemented`.
#   SKIP not configured (it names what is missing and makes no Orgo call), or
#        Orgo refused the size with RAM_ADDON.
# Full runbook, including deleting a leaked box by hand: docs/RESTORE.md §6.
#
# The Orgo API key. A secret: env only, never a settings row. Unset = SKIP.
#ORGO_API_KEY=
# BACKUP_S3_ENDPOINT, BACKUP_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID and BACKUP_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
# are declared in the state-backup topic (140) and must be set on the hub too.
#
# An Orgo template ref you own; the borrowed computer boots from it. No default.
# Unset = SKIP, nothing is spent.
#RESTORE_DRILL_TEMPLATE_REF=
# Path on the hub to the identity that decrypts the restored env (passed to the
# steps). No default.
#RESTORE_DRILL_IDENTITY_FILE=
# Hours between drills. A newer marker exits 0 unless --force. 0 = no guard.
#RESTORE_DRILL_MIN_INTERVAL_H=24
# Seconds the drill waits for the computer to report running before it FAILs.
#RESTORE_DRILL_DEADLINE_S=2700
# Seconds between status polls while waiting.
#RESTORE_DRILL_POLL_S=15
# Size of the borrowed computer. A non-integer FAILs before any call.
#RESTORE_DRILL_RAM_GB=8
#RESTORE_DRILL_CPU=2
# curl -m on every Orgo API call.
#RESTORE_DRILL_CALL_TIMEOUT_S=300
# The project the post-restore smoke checks (passed to the steps).
#RESTORE_DRILL_HEALTH_PROJECT=cromford
# The Orgo API host.
#ORGO_API_BASE=https://www.orgo.ai/api
